---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Webcam Studio Scaling Strategies"
  description="How to scale a webcam studio from 5 to 50+ models without losing traffic quality. Scheduling systems, performance tracking, and regional growth strategies."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Webcam Studio Scaling</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #555; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      The strategies that work for one model break at studio scale. Here's how to grow without losing control.
    </p>

    <h2>Why Scaling Is Hard</h2>
    <p>
      Adding more models to a studio doesn't automatically mean more traffic. Without coordination,
      models compete with each other for the same viewers, creating dead hours and peak-hour cannibalization.
      Scaling requires systems, not just headcount.
    </p>

    <h2>The Three Pillars of Studio Scaling</h2>

    <h3>1. Schedule Architecture</h3>
    <p>
      A well-run studio has coverage during every meaningful traffic window across its target regions.
      We build scheduling frameworks that distribute models across time zones and audience segments
      to maximize aggregate viewer count without internal competition.
    </p>

    <h3>2. Performance Tracking</h3>
    <p>
      You can't optimize what you don't measure. We help studios build simple dashboards that
      track per-model performance, identify top performers, spot declining trends early, and
      understand which audience segments are growing vs. saturating.
    </p>

    <h3>3. Regional Expansion</h3>
    <p>
      Most studios grow by audience depth (more viewers in the same region) before going wide.
      We help identify when it's time to expand regionally and how to target new markets without
      diluting existing performance.
    </p>

    <h2>Studio SEO at Scale</h2>
    <p>
      Studios with 10+ models can build meaningful SEO leverage that individual performers can't.
      We create content strategies that establish your studio as an authority in your niche,
      driving passive traffic from search that supplements platform discovery.
    </p>

    <h2>Let's Talk About Your Studio</h2>
    <p>
      Every studio is different. Tell us where you are now and where you want to go,
      and we'll put together a scaling roadmap that fits your situation.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
